module Core

### Multi-threaded reference-counting controller — the atomic twin of {RetainController[T]}.
### Owns the managed entity; shared between {Shared[T]} (strong) and {Watched[T]} (weak). All
### count mutations go through SeqCst atomic intrinsics driven on the live field address
### (`me.<field>.hijack()`), so cloning/dropping a handle is safe across threads.
### :typeparam T: The exclusively owned entity type.
entity ShareController[T]
needs T is EntityType
  ### Strong reference count (live `Shared` handles). Atomic.
  secret strong_count: U64
  ### Weak reference count (live `Watched` handles). Atomic.
  secret weak_count: U64
  ### Raw pointer to the managed entity.
  secret data: Hijacked[T]

### Creates a new controller with one strong reference and no weak references.
### :param data: The raw pointer to the entity; ownership transfers to this controller.
### :returns: The resulting `ShareController[T]` value.
dangerous routine ShareController[T].$create(data: Hijacked[T]) -> ?ShareController[T]
  return ShareController[T](
    strong_count: 1_u64,
    weak_count: 0_u64,
    data: data
  )

### Atomically increments the strong count when a `Shared` handle is cloned.
routine ShareController[T].increase_strong_count()
  danger!
    discard atomic_add[U64](ptr: me.strong_count.hijack(), value: 1_u64)
  return

### Atomically decrements the strong count. When it reaches zero the managed entity is dropped,
### and the controller itself is freed if no weak handles remain.
routine ShareController[T].decrease_strong_count()
  danger!
    var previous = atomic_sub[U64](ptr: me.strong_count.hijack(), value: 1_u64)
    if previous == 1_u64
      me.drop_data()
      if me.weak_count() == 0_u64
        me.$destroy()
  return

### Atomically increments the weak count when a `Watched` handle is cloned.
routine ShareController[T].increase_weak_count()
  danger!
    discard atomic_add[U64](ptr: me.weak_count.hijack(), value: 1_u64)
  return

### Atomically decrements the weak count, freeing the controller when both counts reach zero.
routine ShareController[T].decrease_weak_count()
  danger!
    var previous = atomic_sub[U64](ptr: me.weak_count.hijack(), value: 1_u64)
    if previous == 1_u64
      if me.strong_count() == 0_u64
        me.$destroy()
  return

### Returns the current number of live strong (`Shared`) handles. Snapshot only.
### :returns: The strong reference count.
routine ShareController[T].strong_count() -> U64
  danger!
    return atomic_load[U64](ptr: me.strong_count.hijack())

### Returns the current number of live weak (`Watched`) handles. Snapshot only.
### :returns: The weak reference count.
routine ShareController[T].weak_count() -> U64
  danger!
    return atomic_load[U64](ptr: me.weak_count.hijack())

### Returns a non-owning pointer to the managed data.
### :returns: The resulting `Hijacked[T]` value.
dangerous routine ShareController[T].borrow_data() -> Hijacked[T]
  return me.data

### Destroys the managed entity. Call only when the strong count reaches zero.
### Runs the entity's own `$destroy` (the sole free under unified teardown); does not also
### `invalidate`, which would double-free a self-freeing entity.
dangerous routine ShareController[T].drop_data()
  me.data.as_entity().$destroy()
  return

dangerous routine ShareController[T].$destroy()
  me.strong_count.$destroy()
  me.weak_count.$destroy()
  me.hijack().invalidate()
  return